# Keep shell scripts checked out as LF.
#
# Blobs in this repository are already stored as LF; core.autocrlf converts
# them to CRLF in the working copy on Windows. A script executed directly
# from a WSL working copy then fails with:
#   /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout deterministic regardless of each
# machine's autocrlf setting, which is what the deploy flow relies on when
# these scripts are run on the origin server.
#
# Scoped to *.sh: line endings in documentation do not affect execution, and
# renormalizing them would produce a large diff for no functional gain.
*.sh text eol=lf
